@startuml paradigm-overview
' The three engines of the paradigm subsystem and the artifacts that flow
' between them. Colour encodes role: code artifacts (orange), topic/analysis
' engines (purple), configuration (slate), results (green).
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/paradigm-overview.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/paradigm/overview.md §2
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontColor #4A148C
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title libgrammstein::topic::paradigm — three independent engines over one code sample  (feature "rag")

rectangle "**Source code**\n.rs · .py · .js · .java\n.rho · .metta" as src #EF6C00
rectangle "**Token stream**\nVec<String>  (analyze_tokens)\n&[&str]  (detect_*_patterns)" as toks #F57C00
rectangle "**API-call sequences**\nVec<Vec<&str>> — one sequence\nper function / trace" as seqs #FB8C00

package "topic::paradigm" {
  rectangle "**ParadigmDetector**\n170 weighted PatternDefs\nOOP · FP · Reactive · Procedural\n→ what //style// is this code?" as det #6A1B9A
  rectangle "**ApiPatternMiner**\nPrefixSpan sequential mining\n→ which call //orders// recur?" as mine #8E24AA
  rectangle "**DomainPatternDetector**\nRholang (14) · MeTTa (22)\n→ which //DSL idioms// occur?" as dom #AB47BC
}

rectangle "**ParadigmConfig**\nweights · context_window\nnormalize_scores" as cfg #546E7A
rectangle "**ApiPatternConfig**\nmin_support · max_gap\nclosed_only · max_patterns" as acfg #546E7A

rectangle "**ParadigmProfile**\n4 scores ∈ [0,1] + indicators\n+ dominant_paradigm()" as prof #2E7D32
rectangle "**Vec<ApiPattern>**\nsequence · support · support_ratio" as apat #2E7D32
rectangle "**Vec<RholangPatternMatch>**\n**Vec<MettaPatternMatch>**\nname · category · position · weight" as dmat #2E7D32

src --> toks : tokenize
src --> seqs : extracted by the caller\n(e.g. from a CPG / AST)

toks --> det
toks --> dom
seqs --> mine

cfg -[#546E7A]-> det
acfg -[#546E7A]-> mine

det --> prof
mine --> apat
dom --> dmat

note bottom of mine
  The miner is **language-agnostic**:
  it consumes any sequence of strings,
  so the caller — not the miner —
  decides what an "API call" is.
end note

note bottom of dom
  Catalogs are **open**: add_pattern()
  extends either catalog at run time.
end note
@enduml
